a = 2s - 10$ ... (D')\n\nNow (C'): $a^2 + ac + c = 10 - 2s$\n(D'): $c^2 + ac + a = 2s - 10$\n\nAdd them: $a^2 + c^2 + 2ac + a + c = 0$\n$(a + c)^2 + (a + c) = 0$\n$(a+c)(a+c+1) = 0$\n\nSo either $a + c = 0$ or $a + c = -1$.\n\nGreat! Let me denote $t = a + c$.\n\nCase 1: $a + c = 0$, so $c = -a$.\nCase 2: $a + c = -1$, so $c = -1 - a$.\n\nAlso from (B): $a(s-6) + c(s-4) = s$.\n$a(s-6) + c(s-4) = (a+c)s - 6a - 4c = s$.\n$(a+c)s - 6a - 4c = s$.\n\nCase 1: $a + c = 0$, $c = -a$:\n$0 \\cdot s - 6a - 4(-a) = s$\n$-6a + 4a = s$\n$-2a = s$\n$a = -s/2$, $c = s/2$.\n\nNow check (C'): $a^2 + ac + c = 10 - 2s$.\n$a^2 + ac + c = a^2 + a(-a) + (-a) = a^2 - a^2 - a = -a = s/2$.\nSo $s/2 = 10 - 2s$, $s/2 + 2s = 10$, $5s/2 = 10$, $s = 4$.\n\nSo $s = 4$, $a = -2$, $c = 2$.\n$b = s - 4 = 0$, $d = s - 6 = -2$.\n$z = -2 + 0i = -2$, $w = 2 - 2i$.\n$zw = (-2)(2 - 2i) = -4 + 4i$.\nCheck: $r = ac - bd = (-2)(2) - (0)(-2) = -4$. $s = ad + bc = (-2)(-2) + (0)(2) = 4$. ✓\n$u = -4 + 4i$.\n\nVerify eq1: $|z|^2 + zw + \\bar{w} = 4 + (-4+4i) + (2+2i) = 2 + 6i$. ✓\nVerify eq2: $|w|^2 + \\overline{zw} + z = (4+4) + (-4-4i) + (-2) = 8 - 4 - 4i - 2 = 2 - 4i$. ✓\n\nCase 2: $a + c = -1$, $c = -1 - a$.\nFrom (B): $(a+c)s - 6a - 4c = s$\n$-s - 6a - 4(-1-a) = s$\n$-s - 6a + 4 + 4a = s$\n$-s - 2a + 4 = s$\n$-2a = 2s - 4$\n$a = 2 - s$, $c = -1 - (2-s) = s - 3$.\n\nNow check (C'): $a^2 + ac + c = 10 - 2s$.\n$a^2 + ac + c = (2-s)^2 + (2-s)(s-3) + (s-3)$\n$= (2-s)^2 + (2-s)(s-3) + (s-3)$\n\nLet me expand:\n$(2-s)^2 = 4 - 4s + s^2$\n$(2-s)(s-3) = 2s - 6 - s^2 + 3s = 5s - 6 - s^2$\n$(s-3) = s - 3$\n\nSum: $4 - 4s + s^2 + 5s - 6 - s^2 + s - 3 = (4 - 6 - 3) + (-4s + 5s + s) + (s^2 - s^2)$\n$= -5 + 2s$\n\nSo $-5 + 2s = 10 - 2s$\n$4s = 15$\n$s = 15/4$\n\nSo $s = 15/4$, $a = 2 - 15/4 = -7/4$, $c = 15/4 - 3 = 3/4$.\n$b = s - 4 = 15/4 - 16/4 = -1/4$, $d = s - 6 = 15/4 - 24/4 = -9/4$.\n$z = -7/4 - i/4$, $w = 3/4 - 9i/4$.\n$zw = (-7/4 - i/4)(3/4 - 9i/4)$\n$= (-7/4)(3/4) + (-7/4)(-9i/4) + (-i/4)(3/4) + (-i/4)(-9i/4)$\n$= -21/16 + 63i/16 - 3i/4 + 9i^2/16$\n\nWait, $(-i/4)(-9i/4) = 9i^2/16 = -9/16$.\n$= -21/16 - 9/16 + (63/16 - 3/4)i$\n$= -30/16 + (63/16 - 12/16)i$\n$= -15/8 + 51i/16$\n\nHmm, let me check $r = ac - bd$:\n$r = (-7/4)(3/4) - (-1/4)(-9/4) = -21/16 - 9/16 = -30/16 = -15/8$. ✓\n$s = ad + bc = (-7/4)(-9/4) + (-1/4)(3/4) = 63/16 - 3/16 = 60/16 = 15/4$. ✓\n\nSo $u = -15/8 + 15i/4$.\n\nVerify eq1: $|z|^2 + zw + \\bar{w}$\n$|z|^2 = (-7/4)^2 + (-1/4)^2 = 49/16 + 1/16 = 50/16 = 25/8$\n$zw = -15/8 + 15i/4$\n$\\bar{w} = 3/4 + 9i/4$\nSum real: $25/8 - 15/8 + 3/4 = 10/8 + 6/8 = 16/8 = 2$. ✓\nSum imag: $15/4 + 9/4 = 24/4 = 6$. ✓\n\nVerify eq2: $|w|^2 + \\overline{zw} + z$\n$|w|^2 = (3/4)^2 + (-9/4)^2 = 9/16 + 81/16 = 90/16 = 45/8$\n$\\overline{zw} = -15/8 - 15i/4$\n$z = -7/4 - i/4$\nSum real: $45/8 - 15/8 - 7/4 = 30/8 - 14/8 = 16/8 = 2$. ✓\nSum imag: $-15/4 - 1/4 = -16/4 = -4$. ✓\n\nSo $S = \\{-4 + 4i, -15/8 + 15i/4\\}$.\n\nNow compute $|u_1|^2 + |u_2|^2$:\n$|u_1|^2 = (-4)^2 + 4^2 = 16 + 16 = 32$.\n$|u_2|^2 = (-15/8)^2 + (15/4)^2 = 225/64 + 225/16 = 225/64 + 900/64 = 1125/64$.\n\nSum: $32 + 1125/64 = 2048/64 + 1125/64 = 3173/64$.\n\nLet me double-check: $32 = 2048/64$. $2048 + 1125 = 3173$. So $3173/64$.\n\n$3173/64 = 49.578125$.\n\nLet me verify $3173$ is not further reducible. $3173 = 64 \\cdot 49 + 37 = 3136 + 37$. $\\gcd(3173, 64)$: $3173 = 49 \\cdot 64 + 37$, $64 = 1 \\cdot 37 + 27$, $37 = 1 \\cdot 27 + 10$, $27 = 2 \\cdot 10 + 7$, $10 = 1 \\cdot 7 + 3$, $7 = 2 \\cdot 3 + 1$. So $\\gcd = 1$. The fraction is already in lowest terms.\n\nThe answer is $\\boxed{3173/64}$.\n\nLet me write up the proof cleanly.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786757431}
